                       "name":  "Reporting hazards, incidents and injuries",
                       "kind":  "progressive-depth",
                       "owner":  "CPCWHS1001",
                       "ownerCluster":  1,
                       "rationale":  "CPCWHS1001 is the White Card - the statutory general construction induction - and is delivered in the first week of Term 1. Hazard and incident reporting is content the induction is required by law to cover, so a learner meets it there before anything else. CPCCWHS2001 follows in the same cluster and goes deeper.",
                       "teachingRule":  "CPCCWHS2001 does not re-teach what a hazard is or why it is reported. It teaches the DELTA: the organisation\u0027s own reporting procedure, the forms and registers that record it, and the notifiable-incident duty that sends a report to the regulator rather than to a supervisor.",
