                       "kind":  "shared-scaffold",
                       "owner":  "CPCCSP2002",
                       "ownerCluster":  3,
                       "rationale":  "Three units require a JSA or SWMS prepared to the Safe Work Australia Code of Practice for Construction Work. CPCCSP2002, first in Term 3, is the earliest of them, and a SWMS is a document a learner writes once and then reuses with a different task in the task column.",
                       "teachingRule":  "CPCCSP2003, CPCCCO2013 and CPCCVE1011 each produce a SWMS for their own task. They are assessed on the CONTENT being right for that task, not on knowing what a SWMS is. The risk-control reasoning behind it belongs to CPCCWHS2001 in Cluster 1 and is cited, not repeated.",
